 "notes": "Trail/log group/alias/role/policy names matched by stated value. Policy statements are bound to the resource the prompt names (bucket policy, named inline role policy, KMS key): planned policy-document data sources via ref, with the planned JSON or __declared__ text as fallbacks when the planned JSON is unknown. Organization-trail toggle: declared is_organization_trail must be set and plan to false (variables resolve to defaults, so the variable itself is not observable). KMS toggle: the key is count/for_each-gated. Accepted alternatives: inline bucket SSE, inline_policy on the role, random_integer for the 12-digit suffix, advanced or omitted event selectors (omitted = all management events). Text fallbacks name the exact action (no wildcard), because the root statement's kms:* and deny-all s3:* statements would otherwise satisfy them; wildcard grants are still accepted through the planned policy-document branch (glob_covers, bound to the principal). Organization-trail toggle: a boolean variable with an org-named name must default to false. PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: the prompt says the trail name and organization flag are controlled by variables, but the GT trail hardcodes name and is_organization_trail = false (the variables are declared but unused), so the trail's use of the variables is not checked. trail_to_loggroup is core, parallel to trail_to_bucket. Known Partial: key-policy text fallbacks (kp_*) are not bound to a principal, so e.g. kp_decrypt can be satisfied by the S3 statement's kms:Decrypt; the planned policy-document branch binds them."
}
